  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Gambia faces mounting environmental and climate challenges, including deforestation, land degradation, biodiversity loss, and coastal erosion. Rising temperatures and erratic rainfall patterns are disrupting agriculture, tourism, fisheries, and public health. Coastal communities are increasingly vulnerable to floods and sea-level rise, highlighting the need for robust disaster risk mitigation.Municipal solid waste generation exceeds 530 tons daily, projected to reach over 1,000 tons by 2030,</narrative>
  </description>
